-- title:
--   Relative degree ψ(p²) of the level-p² divisor-expansion field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a natural number carrying the instance that it is prime, and work inside the field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, in which $j$ is modelled by the element `jq` $= q^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$, the product of the Hahn series $q^{-1}$ with the rational power series obtained from the integral numerator series `jNum` of the $j$-invariant. Let $\mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{jq})$ denote the intermediate field `IntermediateField.adjoin ℚ {jq}`, and let `modularFunctionFieldFull (p * p)` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set of all divisor expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ d\ \mathrm{jq}$ with $d$ a nonzero divisor of $p^2$, i.e. by $j(q)$, $j(q^p)$ and $j(q^{p^2})$. The assertion is that the relative finrank `IntermediateField.relfinrank` of the first field inside the second equals $\mathrm{dedekindPsi}(p^2)$, where $\mathrm{dedekindPsi}(N)=\sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$; for $N=p^2$ this value is $p^2+p$. Thus $[\mathbb{Q}(j(q),j(q^p),j(q^{p^2})):\mathbb{Q}(j(q))]=\psi(p^2)$.
--
--   This is the prime-square case of the classical degree formula for the modular equation: the function field of $X_0(N)$, realised as a subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions of $j$, has degree $\psi(N)$ over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$. It is used in the project's construction of the function field of $X_0(p^2)$ and in the computation of Hecke and Fricke data at level $p^2$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.functionFieldGeneration_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.functionFieldGeneration_sq), [`ModularCurve.heckeAlphaBar_frickeInvolutionBar_sq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeAlphaBar_frickeInvolutionBar_sq) and [`ModularCurve.heckeDivBar_cuspidalDivisor_self_of_prime`](thm.html#ModularCurve.heckeDivBar_cuspidalDivisor_self_of_prime).
-- source:
